                    <TrustBadge />
                </div>
                <h1
                    class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black text-white leading-tight mb-8"
                >
                    The Brutal Truth About <span class="text-[#38BDF8]"
                        >Back Hair</span
                    >: Why Ignoring It Is Destroying Your Confidence
                </h1>
                <p
                    class="text-xl text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-8 max-w-3xl mx-auto"
                >
                    Let’s be honest. Nobody talks about back hair openly—but
                    everyone notices it. Whether you're at the gym, beach, pool,
                    or even just wearing a fitted shirt, back hair silently
                    kills confidence.
                </p>
                <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
                    <a
                        href="#quick-fix"
                        class="px-8 py-4 bg-[#FF4500] hover:bg-[#E63E00] text-white font-black rounded-xl shadow-lg transition-all no-underline"
                    >
                        Find the 5-Minute Fix
                    </a>
                    <a
                        href="#the-mistakes"
                        class="px-8 py-4 bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 text-white font-bold rounded-xl border border-white/10 no-underline"
                    >
                        Read the Truth
                    </a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Content -->
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-16 lg:py-24">
            <div
                class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"
            >
                <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
                    Back hair doesn't just appear overnight. It slowly takes
                    over until removing it becomes frustrating, awkward, and
                    nearly impossible without help.
                </p>

                <!-- Statistics Callout -->
                <div class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8 my-8">
                    <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#38BDF8] mb-4">The Numbers Don't Lie</p>
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 text-center">
                        <div>
                            <p class="text-3xl font-black text-white">50%+</p>
                            <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs mt-1">of men have noticeable back hair</p>
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            <p class="text-3xl font-black text-[#38BDF8]">24%</p>
                            <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs mt-1">groom their back weekly (ages 30-59)</p>
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            <p class="text-3xl font-black text-white">73%</p>
                            <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs mt-1">of young men groom for confidence</p>
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            <p class="text-3xl font-black text-[#FF4500]">47%</p>
                            <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs mt-1">say the back is most neglected</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <p class="text-gray-500 text-[10px] mt-4 text-center">
                        Sources: PMC/SAGE Journals (2017, n=4,198), Statista, LawnStarter 2024 Survey
                    </p>
                </div>

                <p>
                    According to a nationally representative study published in
                    the American Journal of Men's Health (Gaither et al., 2017),
                    over 50% of men report regular body hair grooming — yet the
                    back remains the most neglected area, with nearly half of
                    adults admitting they simply don't address it. The reasons
                    are practical: you can't see it, you can't reach it, and
                    most tools aren't designed for it.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Modern back shavers have completely changed the game. What
                    used to require another person, expensive waxing
                    appointments, or painful trial-and-error can now be done
                    alone—in under 5 minutes. With extended handles reaching
                    18-20 inches and safety-engineered blades, these tools were
                    built for the exact problem you're facing.
                </p>

                <div class="my-12 relative group">
                    <div
                        class="absolute -inset-1 bg-gradient-to-r from-[#1E90FF] to-[#38BDF8] rounded-3xl blur opacity-25 group-hover:opacity-40 transition duration-1000 group-hover:duration-200"
                    >
                    </div>
                    <div
                        class="relative rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border-4 border-white shadow-2xl aspect-video bg-gray-100 flex items-center justify-center"
                    >
                        <img
                            src="/images/blog/blog-img-1.png"
                            alt="The internal struggle of back hair"
                            class="w-full h-full object-cover"
                        />
                        <div
                            class="absolute inset-x-0 bottom-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-black/60 to-transparent p-6 text-white"
                        >
                            <p class="font-bold m-0">
                                True confidence starts with personal control.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div
                    class="bg-gray-50 border-l-4 border-[#1E90FF] p-8 my-12 rounded-r-2xl"
                >
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-0 mb-4">
                        Why Back Hair Is a Bigger Problem Than Most Men Realize
                    </h2>
                    <div class="space-y-6">
                        <div>
                            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">
                                1. It Makes You Look Less Groomed Instantly
                            </h3>
                            <p class="text-gray-600 m-0">
                                Even if you're fit, well-dressed, and clean,
                                visible back hair creates a subconscious
                                impression of poor grooming. People notice, even
                                if they don't say it.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">
                                2. It Traps Sweat, Odor, and Bacteria
                            </h3>
                            <p class="text-gray-600 m-0">
                                Back hair acts like a sponge, trapping sweat,
                                dead skin, and bacteria. This leads to
                                breakouts, skin irritation, and stronger body
                                odor.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">
                                3. Clothes Fit Worse
                            </h3>
                            <p class="text-gray-600 m-0">
                                It creates friction, causing shirts to stick and
                                creating visible outlines through fabric.
                                Shaving makes clothes fit smoother instantly.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">
                                4. It Affects Your Gym Confidence
                            </h3>
                            <p class="text-gray-600 m-0">
                                A 2024 survey found that 73% of men aged 25-34
                                groom specifically for confidence in social and
                                physical settings. If you've ever hesitated
                                to take your shirt off at the gym, pool, or
                                beach — back hair is often the unspoken reason.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">
                                5. It Gets Worse with Age
                            </h3>
                            <p class="text-gray-600 m-0">
                                Testosterone-driven body hair growth typically
                                increases through your 30s and 40s.
                                Back hair that starts as "barely noticeable"
                                in your 20s can become dense coverage by your
                                mid-30s. Starting a grooming routine early
                                makes maintenance simpler long-term.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

