                    chronic low-grade dissatisfaction that affects daily behavior in
                    subtle but measurable ways.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Men who feel self-conscious about their back hair often develop
                    avoidance behaviors without consciously recognizing the pattern.
                    They decline invitations to pool parties, choose baggy shirts over
                    fitted ones, avoid the beach during peak hours, and position
                    themselves strategically in gym locker rooms. These small behavioral
